Track 2: "Where does the copper go?"
- Story & Context: During the long wait between the Omaha junction and the vacuum-lock gate, Sarah leaned over to ask the stranger beside her if he knew why their pockets felt so heavy with magnetized dust. She pressed her ear to the cold, vibrating window pane and heard the track-bed whispering the coordinates of a forgotten star, realizing then that her own heartbeat had synchronized to the mechanical rhythm of the rails. "Tell me true, does the rail lead to the root or the light?" she sang into the dark, her voice a hollow, haunting echo of a thousand late-night travelers.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a human hand holding a handful of glowing, metallic sand that transforms into stardust, dramatic overhead train carriage lighting, moody cinematic depth of field.

Track 3: Hem-Stitched Nebula
- Story & Context: Years after the great de-railment, the locals in the station town of Oakhaven claim they can still hear the collective humming of the Syndicate rising from the rusted tracks at midnight, like a shroud being mended by ghosts. Legend says they didn't crash, but rather wove the train into the orbit of the nearest red giant, creating a permanent, vibrating tether between the earth and the firmament. "We tied the engine to the center of the spinning dark," goes the myth of the commuters who never made it home.
